  Scenario Outline: Grouping Tokens into Lines for Formatting
    The internal `linesForFormat` function should correctly group HCL tokens into `formatLine` structures,
    categorizing them into lead, assign, and comment cells.

    Given the following HCL tokens are lexed:
      | token_type         | token_bytes |
      | ------------------ | ----------- |
      | <token_type_1>     | <bytes_1>   |
      | <token_type_2>     | <bytes_2>   |
      | ...                | ...         |
    When the tokens are processed by `linesForFormat`
    Then the resulting `formatLine` structures should be:
      | line_index | lead_tokens_summary | assign_tokens_summary | comment_tokens_summary |
      | ---------- | ------------------- | --------------------- | ---------------------- |
      | <line_idx> | <lead_summary>      | <assign_summary>      | <comment_summary>      |
      | ...        | ...                 | ...                   | ...                    |

