Feature: HCL Native Syntax Formatting
  This feature covers the canonical formatting of HCL native syntax source code,
  including spacing, indentation, alignment, and comment handling. It also
  covers the internal logic of how tokens are grouped into lines for formatting.

  Background:
    Given a HCL writing context

  Scenario Outline: Canonical HCL Formatting
    The `Format` function should correctly format various HCL constructs.

    Given the following HCL input:
    """
    <input_hcl>
    """
    When the HCL input is formatted
    Then the formatted HCL output should be:
    """
    <expected_hcl>
    """

    Examples:
      | input_hcl                                 | expected_hcl                              |
      |-------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------|
      | ""                                        | ""                                        |
      | "a=1"                                     | "a = 1"                                   |
      | "a=b.c"                                   | "a = b.c"                                 |
      | "a=b[c]"                                  | "a = b[c]"                                |
      | "a=b()[c]"                                | "a = b()[c]"                              |
      | "a=[\"hello\"][0]"                          | "a = [\"hello\"][0]"                        |
      | "( a+2 )"                                 | "(a + 2)"                                 |
      | "( a*2 )"                                 | "(a * 2)"                                 |
      | "( a+-2 )"                                | "(a + -2)"                                |
      | "( a*-2 )"                                | "(a * -2)"                                |
      | "(-2+1)"                                  | "(-2 + 1)"                                |
      | "foo(1, -2,a*b, b,c)"                     | "foo(1, -2, a * b, b, c)"                 |
      | "foo(a,b...)"                             | "foo(a, b...)"                            |
      | "! true"                                  | "!true"                                   |
      | "a=\"hello ${ name }\""                    | "a = \"hello ${name}\""                   |
      | "a=\"hello ${~ name ~}\""                   | "a = \"hello ${~name~}\""                 |
      | "a=\"${b}${c}${ d } ${e}\""                 | "a = \"${b}${c}${d} ${e}\""               |
      | "\"%{if true}${var.foo}%{endif}\""          | "\"%{if true}${var.foo}%{endif}\""        |
      | "b{}"                                     | "b {}"                                    |
      | "\n\"${\nhello\n}\"\n"                      | "\n\"${\n  hello\n}\"\n"                    |
      | "\nfoo(\n1,\n- 2,\na*b,\nb,\nc,\n)\n"      | "\nfoo(\n  1,\n  -2,\n  a * b,\n  b,\n  c,\n)\n" |
      | "a?b:c"                                   | "a ? b : c"                               |
      | "[ [ ] ]"                                 | "[[]]"                                    |
      | "[for x in y : x]"                        | "[for x in y : x]"                        |
      | "[for x in [y] : x]"                      | "[for x in [y] : x]"                      |
      | "\n[\n[\na\n]\n]\n"                       | "\n[\n  [\n    a\n  ]\n]\n"               |
      | "\n[[\na\n]]\n"                           | "\n[[\n  a\n]]\n"                         |
      | "\n[[\n[\na\n]\n]]\n"                     | "\n[[\n  [\n    a\n  ]\n]]\n"             |
      | "\n[[\n[\na\n]]\n]\n"                     | "\n[[\n  [\n    a\n  ]]\n]\n"             | # Degenerate case
      | "\nb {\na = 1\n}\n"                       | "\nb {\n  a = 1\n}\n"                     |
